R418	Addressee Arg1:T290 Arg2:T293	
R419	Speaker Arg1:T268 Arg2:T293	
T294	Quotation 28940 29113	"You must leave that to me. I have already arranged what is to occur. There is only one point on which I must insist. You must not interfere, come what may. You understand?"
R420	Speaker Arg1:T290 Arg2:T294	
R421	Addressee Arg1:T268 Arg2:T294	
T295	Quotation 29114 29135	"I am to be neutral?"
R422	Addressee Arg1:T290 Arg2:T295	
R423	Speaker Arg1:T268 Arg2:T295	
T296	Quotation 29136 29401	"To do nothing whatever. There will probably be some small unpleasantness. Do not join in it. It will end in my being conveyed into the house. Four or five minutes afterwards the sitting-room window will open. You are to station yourself close to that open window."
R424	Speaker Arg1:T290 Arg2:T296	
R425	Addressee Arg1:T268 Arg2:T296	
T297	Quotation 29402 29408	"Yes."
R426	Addressee Arg1:T290 Arg2:T297	
R427	Speaker Arg1:T268 Arg2:T297	
T298	Quotation 29409 29461	"You are to watch me, for I will be visible to you."
R428	Speaker Arg1:T290 Arg2:T298	
R429	Addressee Arg1:T268 Arg2:T298	
T299	Quotation 29462 29468	"Yes."
R430	Addressee Arg1:T290 Arg2:T299	
R431	Speaker Arg1:T268 Arg2:T299	
T300	Quotation 29469 29630	"And when I raise my hand-- so -- you will throw into the room what I give you to throw, and will, at the same time, raise the cry of fire. You quite follow me?"
R432	Speaker Arg1:T290 Arg2:T300	
R433	Addressee Arg1:T268 Arg2:T300	
T301	Quotation 29631 29642	"Entirely."
R434	Addressee Arg1:T290 Arg2:T301	
R435	Speaker Arg1:T268 Arg2:T301	
T302	Quotation 29643 29675	"It is nothing very formidable,"
T303	Entity 29676 29678	he
T304	Cue 29679 29683	said
R436	Speaker Arg1:T303 Arg2:T302	
R437	Cueing Arg1:T304 Arg2:T302	
R438	Addressee Arg1:T268 Arg2:T302	
T305	Quotation 29735 30070	"It is an ordinary plumber's smoke- rocket, fitted with a cap at either end to make it self-lighting. Your task is confined to that. When you raise your cry of fire, it will be taken up by quite a number of people. You may then walk to the end of the street, and I will rejoin you in ten minutes. I hope that I have made myself clear?"
R439	Speaker Arg1:T303 Arg2:T305	
R440	Cueing Arg1:T304 Arg2:T305	
R441	Addressee Arg1:T268 Arg2:T305	
T306	Quotation 30071 30253	"I am to remain neutral, to get near the window, to watch you, and at the signal to throw in this object, then to raise the cry of fire, and to wait you at the corner of the street."
R442	Addressee Arg1:T303 Arg2:T306	
R443	Speaker Arg1:T236 Arg2:T306	
